Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Compound 3a in the original paper is trans-Br(CO)₄W[CNCPh₂], X-ray W–C, C–N and N–C distances are 1.878(5), 1.275(7) and 1.324(7) Å. The C–N–C angle is 135.4(5)°. The three input distances are 1.934, 1.253 and 1.320 Å. The graph uses the W≡C10–N11=C12Ph₂ limiting form for the chain, W=C10=N11–C12⁺Ph₂ can also contribute. The formal charge on W in the SDF follows covalent bond counting, Integer bond orders in one graph do not measure experimental bond order. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 35 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 30 nonmetal covalent bonds: 25 within range, 1 outside range and 4 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 11–12 C-N 1.2534 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

